# Calls whose checks found a method per class (a block checked once per
# member of `A | Q`): an ordinary call, `.:f` and `&:g`, in a file that
# does not know `B`. `B`'s `f(String)`, of the same arity, is an overload,
# never chosen for them; its `g` overrides `A#g` and is (docs/05 §9).
require_relative "by_name/calls"
class B < A
  def f(x: String) -> String = "B#f(String) #{x.upcase}"
  def g -> String = "B#g"
end
p call_f(B.new)
p ref_f(B.new)
p call_f(Q.new)
p ref_f(Q.new)
p gs(B.new)
p gs(Q.new)
p kept(B.new)
p kept(Q.new)

# A member that is a type parameter is told by the class whose method it
# found (its bound's): `T`'s `g` for an `A`, `Q#g` for a `Q`.
def via_param[T <: A](v: T | Q) -> String = v.with { |x| "#{x.g} #{x.:g.call} #{[x].map(&:g).join}" }
p via_param(A.new)
p via_param(B.new)
p via_param(Q.new)

# A class object of a type parameter beside an instance: told apart by a
# class test, the class method found for `T` dispatched on the class.
class Kind
  def self.k -> String = "Kind.k"
end
class SubKind < Kind
  def self.k -> String = "SubKind.k"
end
class Thing
  def k -> String = "Thing#k"
end
def kind_of[T <: Kind](c: Type[T] | Thing) -> String = c.then { |x| x.k }
p kind_of(SubKind)
p kind_of(Thing.new)
